WEBVTT

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.190
<b>Abashiri</b>

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.190
The history of codebreaking

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.100
has also been the history of codebreakers 
being sent to mental hospitals.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.200
The obsessive desire to break codes makes 
them unable to function in daily life.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.650
So I decided that

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:21.790
until we had a certain amount of 
the skins, we shouldn't even start.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.810
But with this many...

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.880
Shall we kidnap someone from the army?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:27.790
No,

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:31.670
it's hard to believe he'd 
use the kind of complex code

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.920
that would require a 
professional cryptographer.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:40.250
He's made it something that his 
daughter Asirpa can decrypt, I'm sure.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:43.860
Hey, Sugimoto.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.310
How do you read this?

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.620
"U."

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.330
Like in "ukai," to go around.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.710
I'll draw it out for you.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.280
Dad told me to go to school 
and study, you know.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:59.230
Our race doesn't have a written language.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.610
We can get by fine without letters.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.230
You think so, too, right, Sugimoto?

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.420
What's wrong, Sugimoto?

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.250
You keep staring at that
 tracing of Gansoku's tattoo.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.260
Did you notice something?

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.970
Sugimoto couldn't crack the code.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.290
He's a moron.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.240
There's something I noticed.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.530
But I won't tell you.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:51.810
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.550
<b>Kushiro</b>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.080
Wow!

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.840
I can carry even more!

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.150
You're so strong!

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.050
I'll carry you, too!

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.460
Ladies, I want you to tell me what this is.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.320
What is this?

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.500
Do you know?

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.720
Some kind of claw? Or part of a plant?

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.680
This was in the hidden 
room in Abashiri Prison.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.130
According to Inudou Shirosuke's information,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:37.730
one of the tattooed prisoners, 
Doi Shinzo, had it on him.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:43.830
Doi Shinzo was captured on the coast of 
Kushiro eight years ago, and imprisoned.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:48.870
I thought this might lead us to him.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.450
You, Ainu yanshuu.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.730
We're looking for a place to stay.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.290
Any ideas?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.760
Follow me.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.970
Do you eat shishamo smelt?

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.670
They swarm the coasts of 
Kushiro this time of year.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:10.390
We Kushiro Ainu don't fish for them normally,

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.960
but my kotan is starving now.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.480
It's good.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.270
Indeed.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.830
By the way, do you know what this is?

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.760
It's from an etupirka.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.200
What?

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.810
A seabird whose name means 
"beautiful beak" in Ainu.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.670
This is the beak.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.920
It's a marker to attract the opposite sex.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.670
After their breeding 
season ends, it falls off.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.430
You know a lot about it.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.260
Japanese don't hunt etupirka.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:55.520
<b>Abashiri</b>

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:55.520
<b>Kushiro</b>

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:55.520
<b>Nemuro</b>

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:49.570
Shishamo can only be caught on 
the Pacific side of Hokkaido.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.090
In the same way, etupirka can 
only be found east of Kushiro,

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.520
in Nemuro.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.040
Nemuro?

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.480
We may be getting closer to them.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.790
You said your name was Kiraushi, right?

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:06.070
Will you take us to the Nemuro Ainu?

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.440
We'll pay.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.990
Sure.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.050
The pay here ain't worth the work.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.440
Make sure you're ready, Ushiyama.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.830
He's even older than you, right?

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:24.410
He should be barely able to walk. 
Do I still have to be careful?

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.610
Doi Shinzo is a fake name.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:32.840
I met him many years ago, in Kyoto.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.760
Yoichiro the Manslayer.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:43.670
A murderer who killed many important 
people in the last days of the shogunate.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.490
<b>Nemuro</b>

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:57.770
<b>Episode Thirty-Two
Manslayer</b>

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.170
Watch where you're going, old man!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.590
You're young. Move out of the way.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.160
What did you say?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.300
You okay, old man?

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.070
Thanks...

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.530
It makes me sick, watching that man.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:25.230
Why's he wearing Ainu clothes, anyway?

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.320
Ainu atsushi dry fast.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.890
You didn't know that?

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.300
You want to fight? Do you?

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.550
Do you have a home or family?

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:52.940
What's your name?

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.620
I don't even remember...

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.690
Call off the job?

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.170
Why now?

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.310
Warden Inudou is dead.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:08.680
Even if you kill Yoichiro the Manslayer, 
there'll be nobody to give him to.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.800
We were hired by the families 
of the people he killed

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.280
at the end of the shogunate.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:17.330
We're not going home empty-handed 
after coming all the way here.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:20.390
Only you can ID his face.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.540
You're sticking with us to the end.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.720
You should hurry, then.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:33.420
I'm not the only guard who's
 been ordered to find him.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:37.720
The families of the men he's 
killed have sent other assassins.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:45.270
This village leader knows the 
Japanese man named Doi Shinzo well.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.520
He says he lived in the kotan.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:53.110
So Yoichiro the Manslayer 
went to Nemuro, then.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:59.800
He came to this kotan 30 years 
ago and married an Ainu woman.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:02.850
He lived in peace in this village,

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:06.670
but eight years ago, a Japanese 
man with a grudge against him

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.940
came and took his wife hostage.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:14.870
He killed the man to get his wife 
back and was sent to Abashiri Prison.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:21.930
But when he found out his wife was sick and 
had little time left to live, he escaped.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:26.150
After he saw her breath her last,
 he left this kotan,

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.220
and now works at a nearby fishery.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:35.790
What's he even doing?

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:37.710
He doesn't work.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.450
He wet his bed this morning.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:43.260
Which means he doesn't have much time left.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:49.740
My old man was the same. One day he 
couldn't get out of bed, and then he died.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:06.120
Hey, what are you doing, old man?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:22.580
Give me a break. I can't have 
you dying right in front of me.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:27.210
Drowning's a horrible way 
to die. I wouldn't do it.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:31.240
Or did you go senile and 
mistake the sea for a bath?

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:37.320
Before I no longer know 
when it's time to die...

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:43.750
Five of these thugs surround me,

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:48.230
so I take the toughest-looking one 
and split his head open with a rock!

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.810
Really?

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:55.780
Sorry, old man, but when you finish 
your lunch, get your things together.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.590
Is there anyone who can come get you?

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:02.240
We want you to leave 
while you can still walk.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.630
Well? Is he in here?

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:17.130
There! That old man!

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.510
Who are you?

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.390
Move!

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.570
You're Yoichiro the Manslayer?

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:36.890
Manslayer?

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:38.700
That senile old man?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.290
You're sure it's him?

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:47.010
He doesn't look like a manslayer to me.

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:51.170
He should have the tattoos from 
Abashiri on his upper body!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.330
Check.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.000
Right.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.040
No way!

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:08.090
Do you remember when you 
killed Ikeda Magoshichiro?

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.600
This is vengeance for my father.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.560
Apologize in hell.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.830
Get in line.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.920
Lots of people want to kill 
Yoichiro the Manslayer.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.160
I'm at the head of the line.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.520
Vice Commander of the Shinsengumi,
 Hijikata Toshizou.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.590
Gunfire!

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:15.460
Someone got there first.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.460
Okay, head to the back.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.960
So you're alone on patrol tonight?

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:27.770
Normally you're walking around 
Kyoto with Okita and Kondou,

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:31.480
acting like you own the place.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:39.070
That's Yoichiro the Manslayer!

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:13.980
Divine punishment!

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:23.190
That's him!

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.740
What? He's...

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.660
Divine punishment!

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.330
Divine punishment!

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:59.730
That old man was strong as hell.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.820
You wanna persuade him to join us?

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:06.040
No, he's already...

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:29.260
Sensei!

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.010
You said that loyalty to the emperor

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:40.100
would make Japan a good country, 
without discrimination by rank!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:44.940
And I believed in you and 
did all your dirty work!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.130
I did all this for you!

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.350
And you won't protect me?

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.840
You're just leaving me to die!

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:03.430
Traitor... Traitor!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.070
I don't wanna commit seppuku.

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:10.260
I don't wanna die like this!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.240
When you look back at history,

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:12.860
what Yoichiro the Manslayer 
believed in may have been right.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:18.220
<b>Shinsengumi</b>

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.280
After the Meiji Restoration,

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:20.250
Japan modernized to allow it to resist 
the European powers and America.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:25.210
And as a result, we defeated 
both China and Russia.

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:31.690
But winning the Russo-Japanese War didn't 
stop Russia's sweep to the south.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:36.400
Japan was no longer able to 
continue the war any further,

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.110
so they were given no reparations,

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:40.240
and instead settled Karafuto.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:44.450
The Meiji government is nearing its limits.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.270
A new method is needed.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:52.400
Hokkaido must become independent 
to protect the north.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:56.690
We must bring in immigrants from overseas 
to make a multicultural nation.

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:01.870
Yoichiro, I'm still fighting for Japan.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:04.680
Hijikata Toshizou...

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:10.550
You were young because time had stopped.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.260
I'm tired.

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:16.260
I've lived too long.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.750
I took this back from Inudou Shirosuke.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:55.130
I'm told the bird it's from can 
only be found in this area.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:18:00.950
My wife gave it to me so 
I wouldn't forget Nemuro.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.290
I'll put an end to your suffering now.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.950
No, just let me be.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:11.610
I'm not worthy of an easy death.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:16.520
I killed so many in the name 
of Japan and its emperor.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.690
I was a tool of the Imperial loyalists.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:25.660
I'm told "Ainu" means "human."

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:32.360
I came to this land, and lived as a human.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.750
It's not fair that I'm 
the only one who could.

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:08.290
I don't regret my fate, 
that I failed to die at Hakodate.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.080
I lived on because I have a job to do.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.040
I can still run.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:18.640
Isn't that right, Gamushin?

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.080
You got it! Great job, Ogata!

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:39.000
I've never seen a pure white humpe.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:42.110
In Karafuto, they call them monihumpe.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.570
Whale, huh?

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.490
Khorosho!

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:53.020
It's best with miso, but I'm sure 
you can't get any in Russia.

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:53.990
Shiraishi...

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:59.850
Huh? Why do you have Sugimoto's miso?

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:02.180
I was just holding on to it.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.930
Since he has so much stuff.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:10.800
Whale soup made from white whale meat,
potatoes, Asirpa's dried Siberian onion

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:15.750
nirinsou, and the miso
she stole from Sugimoto.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:16.740
It's good!

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:19.030
Japanese need miso!

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:23.140
That's the last of Sugimoto's osoma.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.030
Just get some more when we're back in Japan?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.260
It has to be Sugimoto's osoma!

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:31.560
You'll get to eat it again 
eventually, Asirpa-chan.

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:38.880
Hinna, hinna.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:40.350
Hinna.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:43.340
Hinna.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.750
Ogata, did you just say "hinna"?

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:48.090
Can you say it again?

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:48.810
Come on!

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:53.260
You said it, right? You said it, right, Ogata?

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:59.820
So Kiro-chan, how long 
are we staying in Ako?

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.030
A little longer.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:07.390
We're not just going to have an interview 
with this prisoner in Ako Prison, right?

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:12.960
If we help Sofia escape, 
the guards will follow.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.170
Yup.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:19.080
So we'll help all 250 prisoners 
in the prison escape.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:23.500
If they all run, the guards won't 
be able to focus on Sofia.

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:28.260
How are we getting 250 people out of there?

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:32.970
By destroying the walls at multiple points.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.490
And where are we going to get the bombs?

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:37.880
If we do it here, they'll be able to track us.

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:40.520
There.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.280
That building...

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:46.840
A lighthouse.

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:52.590
It's been supplied with explosives, 
in case Japan attacks again.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.220
All that's left to do is wait.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:22:00.430
When they come, 
we'll have everything we need.

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Revolutionary</b>

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:39.190
Next time: "Revolutionary."
